        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "434c4b88-3ade-5544-84df-2736833896c9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Andy Williams, Charles Wesley\n- Products: We Need a Little Christmas, The Andy Williams Christmas Album, Merry Christmas, Christmas Present, I Still Believe in Santa Claus, Hark! The Herald Angels Sing\n- Topics: Christmas songs, adult contemporary music\n\nFacts:\n- In 1739, Charles Wesley wrote \"Hark! The Herald Angels Sing,\" and it first appeared in the collection \"Hymns and Sacred Poems.\"\n- Andy Williams had previously recorded songs later revisited on \"We Need a Little Christmas\" on the 1963 album \"The Andy Williams Christmas Album,\" including \"Away In A Manger,\" \"The Christmas Song (Chestnuts Roasting On An Open Fire),\" \"It's The Most Wonderful Time Of The Year,\" and \"Silent Night.\"\n- Andy Williams had previously recorded \"Mary's Little Boy Child,\" later revisited on \"We Need a Little Christmas,\" on the 1965 album \"Merry Christmas.\"\n- Andy Williams had previously recorded songs later revisited on \"We Need a Little Christmas\" on the 1974 album \"Christmas Present,\" including \"Angels We Have Heard On High,\" \"Hark! The Herald Angels Sing,\" \"I Heard the Bells on Christmas Day,\" and \"What Child Is This.\"\n- Andy Williams had previously recorded \"I'll Be Home for Christmas,\" later revisited on \"We Need a Little Christmas,\" on the 1990 album \"I Still Believe in Santa Claus.\"\n- \"We Need a Little Christmas\" gives an adult contemporary treatment to these previously recorded Christmas songs and includes three songs that Andy Williams had not recorded before.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "eec7825d-af6a-5d2d-9fc3-8a22b0af2e6c",
        "text": "Page: We Need a Little Christmas (album). Sentence: It gives an adult contemporary treatment to songs that Williams had previously recorded for 1963's \"The Andy Williams Christmas Album\" (\"Away In A Manger\", \"The Christmas Song (Chestnuts Roasting On An Open Fire)\", \"It's The Most Wonderful Time Of The Year\", \"Silent Night\"), 1965's \"Merry Christmas\" (\"Mary's Little Boy Child\"), 1974's \"Christmas Present\" (\"Angels We Have Heard On High\", \"Hark!\nPage: We Need a Little Christmas (album). Sentence: The Herald Angels Sing\", \"I Heard the Bells on Christmas Day\", \"What Child Is This\"), and 1990's \"I Still Believe in Santa Claus\" (\"I'll Be Home for Christmas\") and includes three songs that Williams had not recorded before.\nPage: Hark! The Herald Angels Sing. Sentence: \"Hark!\nPage: Hark! The Herald Angels Sing. Sentence: The Herald Angels Sing\" is a Christmas carol that first appeared in 1739 in the collection \"Hymns and Sacred Poems\", having been written by Charles Wesley.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
